## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | IMPORTANT | CHANGELOG.md | ⚠️ important changelog entry documents mechanisms that don t exist in this pr the added changelog text makes two factual claims that are not delivered by this pr 1 download windows latest pointer file — the entry says the windows button s latest link resolves through a static download windows latest pointer file updated by the same workflow neither half is true there is no site download windows latest file in the tree find site path download → empty no workflow step in build windows yml writes any pointer grep n pointer download windows github workflows build windows yml → no matches and no code fetches resolves through such a file the button links directly to https github com istin flutter agent harness releases latest download fa app windows x64 zip — self sufficient via the stable asset name exactly like the existing chrome extension link no pointer mechanism exists for any platform on fa1 dev 2 site tests extended to pin the new markup — no test site dart test and no check in scripts site mobile check mjs references the windows block grep rn windows download windows msix test site scripts site github → only site index html matches the only pin is the re baked full page reg golden which pins pixels not markup ids why this matters the changelog is shipped repo documentation — future maintainers looking for the pointer file or the markup test will find neither the behavior itself is fine as shipped the direct stable name link doesn t need the pointer the fix is to correct the entry to describe what actually ships e g gains a windows button linking directly to the stable releases latest download fa app windows x64 zip asset markup pinned by the re baked full page golden — or actually add the pointer mechanism if it was intended the pr description repeats the same two claims plus drift flutter 3 47 8 vs the pinned 3 50 0 identity fa fa vs the script s dev fa1 app fa win10 14393 vs the manifest s minversion 10 0 17763 0 — please align the description with the tree as well |
| F2 | open | IMPORTANT | scripts/msix/make_msix.ps1 | ⚠️ important wide310x150logo slot references a 150×150 asset — out of contract manifest reference line 83 points the wide tile slot at the square logo xml uap defaulttile wide310x150logo assets square150x150logo png square150x150logo png is 150×150 ihdr verified but the slot s documented contract is a wide image — microsoft learn uap defaulttile schema learn microsoft com element uap defaulttile https learn microsoft com en us uwp schemas appxpackage uapmanifestschema element uap defaulttile wide310x150logo — the 310x150 wide version of the logo image the other three slots are dimension exact 150×150 44×44 storelogo 50×50 verified against the committed pngs — only the wide slot reuses the wrong square asset note that neither makeappx pack nor signtool sign validates logo pixel dimensions so ci and the local pack sign verification in the pr description cannot catch this the failure mode — if any — appears only at add appxpackage registration time manifest resource validation typically 0x80080204 … does not have the expected dimensions 310x150 or if the os tolerates it as a wrong aspect stretched tile since the msix is a headline artifact of this pr and the install path is unverified the pr description s verification covers pack sign not add appxpackage please either 1 generate a dedicated 310×150 wide logo scripts msix assets wide310x150logo png and reference it or 2 drop the wide310x150logo attribute the tile then stays square format only — acceptable for a utility app and confirm a real add appxpackage import cer → add msix on a clean machine if the install is refused this becomes blocking — please report the repro result on the thread |
| F3 | open | IMPORTANT | scripts/site_mobile_check.mjs | ⚠️ important whole file crlf flip of site mobile check mjs and site mobile yml — 780 lines of silent churn this pr s commits rewrote both files with crlf line endings in the committed blobs scripts site mobile check mjs — 65 65 lines now crlf origin main blob 0 cr bytes github workflows site mobile yml — 123 123 lines now crlf origin main blob 0 cr bytes the substantive change in these two files is 48 −1 the re bake lane the python3 override the raw diff is 78 −741 — everything else is the line ending flip consequences every future git blame archeology on these files now stops at this commit for lines the pr didn t really touch the pr diff carries 780 lines of noise burying the real change it silently contradicts the repo s eol discipline — gitattributes pins crlf only for bat cmd with a written rationale everything else is lf and no rule covers mjs yml so the crlf persists in the blob a future text auto attribute or any lf normalizing tooling will turn these two files into permanent phantom full file diffs no runtime breakage node tolerates crlf the yaml block scalars are line break normalized by every parser so this is not blocking — but the flip is undocumented neither the commit message nor the pr description mentions it please restore lf for both files before merge with ignore cr at eol applied first the resulting diff shrinks to the real 48 −1 change |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

