⚠️ **IMPORTANT (re-raise of round-1 finding F3 — still present, re-verified on head `b092552c8`)**

Both churned files are still committed with CRLF blobs:

- `scripts/site_mobile_check.mjs` — 65/65 lines now CRLF (`origin/main` blob: 0 CR bytes)
- `.github/workflows/site-mobile.yml` — 123/123 lines now CRLF (`origin/main` blob: 0 CR bytes)

Re-verified numbers on this head: the substantive change in these two files is **+48/−1** (the `workflow_dispatch` re-bake lane + the `PYTHON3` override); the raw diff is **+78/−741** — everything else is the line-ending flip. Consequences are unchanged:

- every future `git blame` on these files stops at this commit for lines the PR didn't really touch;
- the PR diff carries ~780 lines of noise, burying the real change;
- it silently contradicts the repo's EOL discipline — `.gitattributes:6-7` pins CRLF **only** for `*.bat`/`*.cmd` (with a written rationale); nothing covers `*.mjs`/`*.yml`, so the CRLF persists in the blob;
- a future `* text=auto` attribute or any LF-normalizing tooling will turn these two files into permanent phantom full-file diffs.

No runtime breakage (node tolerates CRLF; YAML block scalars are line-break-normalized by every parser), so this is not blocking — but the flip remains undocumented. Please restore LF for both files before merge; with `--ignore-cr-at-eol` applied first, the resulting diff shrinks to the real +48/−1 change.

